1. SQL / NoSQL Injection Defense
Neutralizes MongoDB expression operators ($where, $gt, $regex) and enforces Mongoose parameterized schema casting.

2. Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
Applies HTML entity escaping to all user inputs before persistence or rendering, disarming <script> and event handler injections.

3. CSRF & JWT Mitigation
Employs stateless HMAC-SHA256 JWT tokens delivered via HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookies.

